[1m[38;5;231mHow should the daily total appear in the exported CSV and JSON?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mOmit in CSV, field in JSON (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mCSV is pure account rows; JSON is {"day", "rows", "total_cents"}. Cleanest per-format contract.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Separate field/row in both
     [38;5;246mJSON total_cents plus a trailing total row in CSV. Consistent across formats; the CSV row can confuse parsers.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Omit from both
     [38;5;246mBoth files are just account rows; consumers sum. Smallest contract; adding a total to CSV later is breaking.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m Mirror the text output
     [38;5;246mA record with account "total" in both formats. Matches the email exactly; ambiguous for machines.[39m
  [38;5;246m5. Type something.[39m
